Dwayne The Rock Johnson has promised the  hierarchy of power is about to change in  the dceu but who exactly is Black Adam  and how does he fit into the series  timeline here's everything we know about  this anti-heroes history and his future  warning spoilers ahead here we go  possibly the oldest DC EU character to  date Black Adam was born 5 000 years ago  likely predating even Wonder Woman's  birth teth Adam began as a slave of the  fictional country conduct where he lost  his son who died saving his father in  the comics the wizard Shazam grants teth  Adam the powers of gods not knowing that  the former slave holds no restraint in  delivering deadly Justice to his abusers  in Black Adam's original comic book  origin from faucet Comics which takes  place before the character was acquired  by DC he destroys the Pharaoh and condox  Elite before claiming the throne for  himself  after black Adam's Rampage in condoc the  Wizard realizes his mistake in bestowing  teth Adam with the powers of gods unable  to remove his powers Shazam renames the  violent being Black Adam and banishes  him from the world of mankind in the  original faucet origin the wizard  teleports Black Adam to the other side  of the universe forcing the villain to  spend the next 5 000 years flying back  to Earth however the film's teaser shows  the wizard Shazam using his magic to  seemingly entomb Black Adam for  thousands of years giving him time to  find a new champion in the modern day  humans free the demigod who awakens in a  Strange New World  by the time Black Adam escapes his tomb  the citizens of the dceu have already  experienced plenty of bizarre and  dangerous threats aliens from Krypton  tried to destroy the world a beast known  as doomsday nearly destroyed metropolis  and killed Superman Atlantean armies  fought over whether or not to destroy  life on the surface world the  enchantress nearly toppled Midway City a  giant starfish named staro visited  Terror upon Cordo Maltese and alien  butterflies threatened to take over the  world thankfully Humanity lives in an  era of superheroes who can combat such  threats HBO Max's Peacemaker series  offers a clue as to when Black Adam  emerges into this age of Heroes in the  fourth episode the anti-hero Vigilante  gets himself arrested to get thrown into  prison and kill peacemaker's father in a  courtyard where guards are having lunch  one guard is seen reading a newspaper  with an article indicating an  organization known as intergang has  seized power in the nation of Conduct in  DC Comics intergang is a criminal  organization that uses Advanced Weaponry  obtained from the alien planet  apocalypse to further their agenda since  Black Adam considers himself the  protector of conduct once he returns  he'll definitely want to have a few  words with inner Gang This suggests  Black Adam will occur sometime after  Peacemaker  in comic book lore there have been  several versions of Black Adam and his  origins in Shazam volume 1 written by DC  Comics Maestro Jeff Johns we learned  Black Adam is imprisoned by the wizard  in a tomb for his evil Deeds much like  in the movie while researching the  villain shazam's current champion Billy  Batson gets a glimpse into the past and  Witnesses a boy named Amman trying to  survive oppression along with his uncle  the boy is given Powers by the wizard  Shazam and Billy incorrectly assumes  Amman becomes Black Adam however he  later learns amman's Uncle steals his  nephew's power kills the Wizard's  intended champion and transforms into  Black Adam in the Modern Age Dr Savannah  uncovers the entrance to Black Adam's  prison he says the magic word Shazam and  freeze Black Adam who goes in search of  Billy Batson in an attempt to defeat him  and become the ultimate Champion the new  DC EU film makes changes to the comic  book origin focusing on teth Adam's  relationship with his son not his nephew  the movie also doesn't feature Shazam or  his young counterpart to he bouncing  however Black Adam does get released  from his magical prison to bring his  brand of Justice down on those he deems  deserving of his rage this puts him in  conflict with many of Earth's Heroes  including some new faces  black Adam's primary antagonists will be  the Justice Society of America the JSA  is a group of Heroes who came together  during DC's golden age of comics in the  1940s in many DC continuities the JSA  predates the Justice League and clashed  with the enemies of its era including  the tyrannical Nazi regime while JSA  members have all appeared in modern  Comics the JSA is typically recognized  as a superhero team from a classic ERA  with much older Heroes only thing we can  learn from these geezers is how to add  more fiber to our diets the JSA includes  famous members such as the original  flash Jay Garrick as well as the first  human Green Lantern Alan Scott however  Black Adam will focus on other JSA  members including Hawkman Dr Fate Adam  Smasher and Cyclone how these Heroes  came to be in the DC EU is unknown  unlike Superman or Wonder Woman we  haven't received an origin tale for any  of these Heroes however if they're  anything like their comic book  counterparts Dr 8 and Hawkman are both  born from ancient Powers Dr Fate is the  creation of a cosmic deity while Hawkman  was the Egyptian prince Khufu who after  being killed with a mystical dagger is  bound to be reincarnated upon death  during the JSA era Hawkman is reborn as  Carter Hall who adopts the mantle of  Hawkman using alien anti-gravity and  metal to power his armor and weaponry as  for atom smasher he's the heroic  grandson of the super villain cyclotron  in the comics gifted with super strength  and the ability to control the size and  density of his body meanwhile Cyclone is  the granddaughter of the original Red  Tornado and possesses the powers of  flight wind control and sound wave  control both are Legacy Heroes with  strong ties to the JSA  Black Adam occurs primarily in the  modern day after the events of the  theatrical released Justice League this  means the JSA and Justice League coexist  in the same era however this doesn't  explain why the JSA are the only Heroes  who seem to be responding to the  climactic events after Black Adam  emerges from his prison while the  Justice League took some time to come  together its individual members have  been active for years cal-el revealed  himself years ago as Superman while  Black Adam was still stuck in limbo  Wonder Woman made herself known to  humanity during the first world war  Bruce Wayne has been operating as Batman  for decades and both Aquaman and the  Flash had superhero careers long before  joining the Justice League the greater  dceu is familiar with these rock stars  but the JSA still seems relatively  unknown it'll be interesting to see how  the timelines link up and learn what the  Justice League is doing when Black Adam  makes himself known notably Amanda  Waller from dceu's suicide Squad films  is working with the JSA and has some  pull with Certain Justice League members  including a certain famous Kryptonian  empowered by the gods themselves Black  Adam is an insanely powerful being and  what better way to show this by having  him challenge the alpha of DC  Superheroes Superman in DC Comics Black  Adam has always been a formidable Foe  for powerhouses like Superman and Shazam  notably aside from Kryptonite Superman  is vulnerable to Magic something Black  Adam can produce punishing amounts of  thanks to his Divine gifts after a  Twitter fan expressed a desire to see  these two Titans come together Johnson  retweeted the message and shared that he  always aims to listen to his audience I  hear you and I always got you state of  the Rock in the film's mid-credits scene  we see Johnson make good on his promise  after being informed by Amanda Waller  that he is not to leave condox borders  Black Adam arrogantly informs her that  no one can stop him from doing what he  wants in response Waller sends Superman  to confront Black Adam who informs the  demigod that they should talk no word on  whether or not this will lead to a big  screen battle between the two but with  Henry Cavill back in the Superman suit  will likely be seeing more of both the  hero and the anti-hero  Shazam and Black Adam are like the Joker  and Batman young Billy Batson as the  all-powerful hero Shazam seeks to do  good and uphold a heroic standard Black  Adam doesn't live by a code of any kind  his goal is singular in his mind and no  Act is too amoral or dicey if it  furthers his objective of obliterating  tyranny and opposition yet despite these  moral differences Shazam and Black Adam  are ultimately two sides of the same  coin imbued with Godly Powers by the  same wizard in the comics the wizard saw  the error of his ways and banished Black  Adam until a hero could be called  forward to defeat him with the rise of  Billy Batson and Shazam that time had  come however this is a film focused on  the bad guy a move meant to position  Black Adam as a sympathetic anti-hero  Shazam is nowhere to be seen and  director John McCool at Sarah said not  to expect a Shazam Black Adam match up  just yet in an interview with variety he  stated our movie is an original story by  the time the movie ends he doesn't know  who she Shazam where Superman is however  it's fairly certain that Black Adam  takes place after the first Shazam film  if Black Adam were around during the  events of Shazam he would have most  certainly confronted Billy over his  powers Black Adam doesn't want a  champion standing in the way of his  goals and wants to be a supreme power  eliminating Shazam is the only means to  that end the two will inevitably meet in  the DCU however even if it isn't in  Black Adam's first outing it's Destiny  while Shazam won't appear in Black Adam  audiences will be seeing Billy Batson's  super powered alter ego very soon Shazam  Fury of the Gods is set to release in  March 2023 just a couple of months after  Black Adam instead of Black Adam however  the sequel will feature a wildly new  antagonist in the form of Helen mirren's  espera a jealous God seeking the power  of Shazam for herself with Black Adam  busy contending with intergang and  kondok and Shazam working with his  family to dispel evil on the other side  of the world in Philly it's it's  unlikely that these two will come to  blows it also remains to be seen if  either film will tease a future Clash or  if either character cameos in the  opposite film from a timeline  perspective however consider these films  either happening concurrently or  relatively close together allowing the  two Champions to remain separate for now  with the future of the Justice League up  in the air there may be a brand new  world for Black Adam to conquer in the  dceu Ben Affleck is wrapping up his time  as Batman with the upcoming The Flash  movie it's hard to believe Ray Fisher  will be back in cyborg anytime soon  after his Feud with Warner Brothers and  the Flash as portrayed by Ezra Miller  will almost definitely not return  outside of his solo project after the  actor's various alleged crimes meanwhile  Wonder Woman is primed for a third film  rounding out a Trilogy for the Amazonian  Warrior Aquaman and the lost kingdom is  also in the works while Henry cavill's  involvement is Superman and future DC EU  movies has been confirmed with that  post-credits scene with Black Adam about  to make his Mark in the dceu could  Johnson's take on the man in Black be  the one that leads us into the future of  dceu the remaining Heroes Aquaman Wonder  Woman Shazam and whoever from the JSA  survives Black Adam could use a central  hero or a unifying villain the film  universe is on the precipice of a  shake-up as Warner Brothers other seems  bent on abandoning what Zack Snyder  began with a leading man like Johnson  Anything is Possible  [Music]
 

